id: pm-rust-ing0
title: Match PM CLI 2026.9.4 event classification and immutable history-record hashes
description: "The required differential conformance test fails against published PM CLI 2026.9.4 on the first create operation. Native history omits event_class, record_hash_version and record_hash; item snapshot hashes already match. Implement the published immutable-record envelope in native Rust and update differential and release tooling to the same published CLI. Preserve the independent native implementation and compare complete persisted bytes."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: conformance,history,rust
created_at: "2026-09-04T19:56:23.648Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T20:06:50.659Z"
assignee: codex-pm-services
claim_principal: codex-pm-services
author: codex-pm-services
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Real differential tests match complete item and history bytes against PM CLI 2026.9.4; record classification distinguishes maintenance from substantive operations; record hashes cover author and provenance; strict Rust checks and the existing exact coverage gate pass
risk: high
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T20:06:50.659Z",codex-pm-services,"The existing full-byte differential acceptance failed before implementation on missing event_class, record_hash_version and record_hash. After the native implementation, it passes against published PM CLI 2026.9.4. All 146 tests pass with the published CLI required, including branch-merge and differential suites. LLVM reports 1691/1691 lines, 159/159 functions, 2363/2363 regions and 278/278 branches covered; no exclusions or thresholds were relaxed. Strict clippy, private-item rustdoc, cargo audit, PM strict health, and pm-changelog regeneration/check also pass. Review remains pending; npm/crate publication stays disabled."
